summary: SIGUSR1 during startup causes recvmsg EINTR crash
description: |
    Sending SIGUSR1 (e.g. dumping stats via fapolicyd-cli -D) while a
    trust database reload is in progress causes recvmsg to return
    -1/EINTR, crashing the daemon with "recvmsg failed". Signal
    handlers are installed with sa_flags=0 (no SA_RESTART).

    The test freezes the rpm-loader child with SIGSTOP to keep the
    daemon blocked in recvmsg, sends SIGUSR1, then unfreezes the
    loader with SIGCONT. This makes the race deterministic.
contact: Renaud Métrich <rmetrich@redhat.com>
test: ./runtest.sh
require+:
  - library(ControlFlow/Cleanup)
  - fapolicyd
duration: 10m
enabled: true
tag:
  - Tier3
tier: '3'
link:
  - verifies: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHEL-189482
adjust+:
  - enabled: false
    when: distro == rhel-4, rhel-5, rhel-6, rhel-7, rhel-8
    because: fapolicyd-rpm-loader does not exist there
  - enabled: false
    when: distro >= rhel-9 and distro < rhel-9.8
    because: the fix is not yet available there
  - enabled: false
    when: distro >= rhel-10 and distro < rhel-10.2
    because: the fix is not yet available there
id: 23304c4d-33ba-434e-9eeb-09658e9c4906
